From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lena <lena@x>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] lena-0142: heartbeat keeps beating after load_init_program

0140 stopped the heartbeat thread at "starting init", exactly where the
boot moved to userspace and where stalls are now happening. Keep it running
for 10 minutes, tagged bsd_init/userspace, so a blocked thread can still be
told from a dead SoC during launchd.
---
diff --git a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
index 4644d64..d9f5acd 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
@@ -476,13 +476,17 @@ sweet_diag_heartbeat(void *arg, wait_result_t wr)
 
 	(void)arg;
 	(void)wr;
-	while (sweet_diag_stage < 2 && secs < 600) {
+	/*
+	 * 0142: keep beating after load_init_program(): before it the thread
+	 * told "blocked in bsd_init" from "SoC dead"; after it the same is true
+	 * for the userspace phase (launchd, backboardd), which is where the boot
+	 * now lives. Stops after 10 minutes so it does not run forever.
+	 */
+	while (secs < 600) {
 		IOSleep(10000);
 		secs += 10;
-		if (sweet_diag_stage >= 2) {
-			break;
-		}
-		printf("SWEET HB: alive %u s (bsd_init)\n", secs);
+		printf("SWEET HB: alive %u s (%s)\n", secs,
+		    sweet_diag_stage < 2 ? "bsd_init" : "userspace");
 	}
 }
 
